# Directory Structure and File Organization

This document outlines the complete directory structure, file organization patterns, and important files/folders in this React TypeScript project with Tailwind CSS v4 and Shadcn/ui components.

## Project Overview

- **Framework**: React 19.1.0 with TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4.1.7 (CSS-first configuration)
- **UI Components**: Shadcn/ui pattern with manual component integration
- **Build Tool**: Vite 6.3.5
- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit with RTK Query
- **Routing**: React Router DOM v7.6.0
- **Internationalization**: i18next with react-i18next
- **Testing/Documentation**: Storybook

## Root Level Structure

```
/
├── package.json              # Main dependencies and scripts
├── tsconfig.json             # Main TypeScript configuration
├── tsconfig.app.json         # App-specific TypeScript config
├── tsconfig.node.json        # Node-specific TypeScript config
├── vite.config.ts            # Vite build configuration
├── components.json           # Shadcn/ui configuration (if exists)
├── eslint.config.mjs         # ESLint configuration
├── postcss.config.mjs        # PostCSS configuration for Tailwind CSS v4
├── .env.template             # Environment variables template
├── index.html                # HTML entry point
├── README.md                 # Project documentation
└── LICENSE                   # License file
```

## Source Code Structure (`src/`)

### Main Application Files

```
src/
├── main.tsx                  # Application entry point
├── App.tsx                   # Root application component
├── vite-env.d.ts            # Vite environment types
├── global.d.ts              # Global TypeScript declarations
└── config.ts                # Application configuration
```

### Assets (`src/assets/`)

```
assets/
├── css/
│   └── main.css             # Main CSS file with Tailwind v4 imports
└── images/
    └── react.svg            # Static images
```

**Key Points:**
- `main.css` contains Tailwind CSS v4 `@import` directives
- Custom CSS and `@theme` configurations go in `main.css`
- Static assets organized by type (css, images, fonts)

### Components (`src/components/`) - Atomic Design Structure

```
components/
├── atoms/                  # Basic UI elements
│   ├── Button.tsx          # Base button component
│   ├── Button.stories.tsx  # Storybook stories
│   └── icons/              # Icon components
│       └── CaretCircleRight.tsx
├── molecules/              # Composite components (empty initially)
├── organisms/              # Complex components (empty initially)
└── templates/              # Page templates (empty initially)
```

**Naming Conventions:**
- **Shadcn Components**: Always use PascalCase (e.g., `Button.tsx`, not `button.tsx`)
- **Icons**: PascalCase with descriptive names
- **Stories**: Component name + `.stories.tsx` suffix
- Follow atomic design hierarchy: atoms → molecules → organisms → templates

### Hooks (`src/hooks/`)

```
hooks/
└── login/
    └── useValidateLoginForm.hook.ts    # Form validation hook
```

**Naming Pattern:**
- `use[FeatureName][Purpose].hook.ts`
- Organized by feature/domain
- Custom hooks for form validation, API calls, state management

### Layouts (`src/layouts/`)

```
layouts/
├── index.tsx               # Main layout exports
├── header.tsx              # Header layout component
└── sidebar.tsx             # Sidebar layout component
```

**Purpose:**
- Reusable layout components
- Header, sidebar, footer structures
- Layout composition and routing integration

### Library Utilities (`src/lib/`)

```
lib/
└── utils.ts                # Utility functions (cn, clsx, etc.)
```

**Contains:**
- `cn()` function for conditional styling with `tailwind-merge`
- Utility functions shared across components
- Helper functions for data manipulation

### Internationalization (`src/locales/`)

```
locales/
├── i18n.tsx               # i18next configuration
├── i18next.d.ts           # i18next TypeScript declarations
├── kr.json                # Korean translations
├── en.json                # English translations
├── ja.json                # Japanese translations
└── vi.json                # Vietnamese translations (default)
```

**Rules:**
- Always define new keys in `vi.json` first
- Use consistent key naming conventions
- Organize keys by feature/page sections

### Models/Types (`src/models/`)

```
models/
└── auth.model.ts          # Authentication-related types
```

**Purpose:**
- TypeScript interfaces and types
- API response models
- Domain-specific type definitions
- Organized by feature/domain

### Pages (`src/pages/`)

```
pages/
├── home.page.tsx          # Home page component
├── private.page.tsx       # Private/protected page
├── auth/
│   └── login.page.tsx     # Login page
└── errors/
    ├── 403.page.tsx       # Forbidden error page
    ├── 404.page.tsx       # Not found error page
    └── 504.page.tsx       # Server error page
```

**Naming Pattern:**
- `[pageName].page.tsx`
- Organized by feature/domain
- Error pages in dedicated `errors/` folder

### Routing (`src/routes/`)

```
routes/
├── index.tsx              # Main routing configuration
├── auth.route.tsx         # Authentication routes
├── errors.route.tsx       # Error page routes
├── home.route.tsx         # Home page routes
└── private/
    ├── index.tsx          # Private routes exports
    └── private.route.tsx  # Protected routes
```

**Organization:**
- Route definitions separate from components
- Grouped by access level (public, private)
- Feature-based route organization

### Services/API (`src/services/`)

```
services/
├── base.ts                # Base API configuration
└── auth.service.ts        # Authentication API services
```

**Purpose:**
- RTK Query API slice definitions
- Base API configuration (endpoints, headers)
- Service layer for external API calls

### WebSocket (`src/sockets/`)

```
sockets/
└── base.ts                # WebSocket base configuration
```

**Purpose:**
- Socket.io client configuration
- Real-time communication setup
- WebSocket event handling

### State Management (`src/store/`)

```
store/
├── index.ts               # Store configuration and exports
└── auth/
    ├── auth.slice.ts      # Redux auth slice
    └── auth.selector.ts   # Redux auth selectors
```

**Organization Pattern:**
- Feature-based state organization
- Separate slice and selector files
- RTK slices with type safety

